      "start_seconds": 0.87,
      "end_seconds": 2.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "evening. Let's get started"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.57,
      "end_seconds": 6.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.78,
      "end_seconds": 10.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Have you been here before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.67,
      "end_seconds": 16.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "A couple of times, but not recently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.16,
      "end_seconds": 18.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "What's been worrying you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.44,
      "end_seconds": 30.63,
      "duration_seconds": 11.19,
      "text": "well, um, I've been having a discharge from the ear it's the not knowing that gets to me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.68,
      "end_seconds": 36.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.44,
      "end_seconds": 42.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Um, you know, it's been going on for ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.21,
      "end_seconds": 46.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Okay, any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.5,
      "end_seconds": 54.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "Okay, uh, so it usually comes with a blocked feeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.35,
      "end_seconds": 57.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.0,
      "end_seconds": 62.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.22,
      "end_seconds": 65.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.79,
      "end_seconds": 69.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.07,
      "end_seconds": 73.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.82,
      "end_seconds": 78.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.34,
      "end_seconds": 80.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.67,
      "end_seconds": 86.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.01,
      "end_seconds": 92.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.92,
      "end_seconds": 97.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Mm, it's glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.31,
      "end_seconds": 102.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.0,
      "end_seconds": 112.38,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "sorry, what was I saying, I've got diabetes. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.38,
      "end_seconds": 124.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.97,
      "end_seconds": 130.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "Yes, diclofenac, it it gives me swelling of my lips."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.04,
      "end_seconds": 142.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "alright, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.76,
      "end_seconds": 146.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "No surgery, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.43,
      "end_seconds": 154.94,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "Any swelling behind the ear, ringing in the ear, facial weakness or recent swimming at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.53,
      "end_seconds": 164.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.96,
      "text": "I haven't had swelling behind the ear, ringing in the ear, facial weakness or recent swimming, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.13,
      "end_seconds": 168.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "and your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.78,
      "end_seconds": 175.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.16,
      "end_seconds": 180.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.84,
      "end_seconds": 184.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.17,
      "end_seconds": 189.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.95,
      "end_seconds": 204.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.82,
      "end_seconds": 227.21,
      "duration_seconds": 8.39,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 98 percent, pressure 114 over 78, pulse is 64 beats a minute, temperature 37.0."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.11,
      "end_seconds": 233.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.02,
      "end_seconds": 237.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.48,
      "end_seconds": 254.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "the ear canal is red and swollen with some debris, and it's painful when I pull the ear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.85,
      "end_seconds": 271.48,
      "duration_seconds": 13.63,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. Okay, thinking it through, I'd lean towards an outer ear canal infection. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.68,
      "end_seconds": 310.12,
      "duration_seconds": 22.44,
      "text": "You'll be taking antibiotic and steroid ear drops, 3 drops, twice a day, for seven days. That's for ear canal infection. Keep the ear dry, no swimming, and don't poke anything into it. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.47,
      "end_seconds": 325.65,
      "duration_seconds": 15.18,
      "text": "Ah. Please don't wait if the ear swells or you get dizzy or feverish. That's when to be seen urgently. Come back if it isn't better in three days. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.13,
      "end_seconds": 337.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "Right, you know, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}